-- name    : ThreeSum.EncodedColorReportingData.report_le_source_allocation
-- status  : Proved
-- author  : @wurtle
-- created : 2026-10-14T16:38:29.807979+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/9ad2b0ac-8042-496e-abe4-2f5f169fc2af
-- title:
--   The reporting base lies inside the allocated source workspace
-- statement:
--   Let $n>0$, let $x$ be an integer input of length $n$, and fix a coloring of width $\lfloor\log_2 n\rfloor+1$. Suppose memory at free base $f$ satisfies the encoded color pipeline's stored-data contract for strictly increasing normalized lists $A,B,C$. Let $q$ be the pipeline's finish address, and let $C(n,U)$ be the cell requirement of the encoded color resource record for an arbitrary natural parameter $U$.
--
--   The reporting base, defined as $q+8$, satisfies
--   $$q+8\le f+C(n,U).$$
--   No additional bound on the input values is assumed in this address comparison.
--
--   This locates the start of reporting within the common source allocation and allows later reporting resources to be attached to the stored pipeline data.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/EncodedColorReportingData.lean#L44-L60

